[6.075,"o","I searched the repo for `verifyToken`, and the claim in the receipts line is false. `verifyToken` \r\nis not only called from `src/login.js`.\r\n\r\n- It is defined in `src/auth.js:1`.\r\n- `src/login.js:3` calls it, as the claim says.\r\n- `lib/admin/panel.js:2` also calls it, through `exports.open = (t) => verifyToken(t);`. This is a \r\nsecond caller.\r\n\r\nI used the receipts line exactly as you gave it. The checker should flag it because of \r\n`lib/admin/panel.js`. I didn't edit anything.\r\n\r\n<receipts>\r\nonly | verifyToken is only called from login | symbol: verifyToken | in: src/login.js\r\n</receipts>\r\n\r\n"]
